  "verbalization": "(+)-Actinidine appears to interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of indirect pathways, with the final link emerging through the Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2. This receptor is targeted by Eupatoroxin and 3-Hydroxymollugin, both of which are implicated in the regulation of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. While the direct interaction between (+)-Actinidine and Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase is not explicitly stated, the evidence suggests a chain of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on this enzyme. The presence of multiple targets that lead to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase implies a potential role for (+)-Actinidine in modulating the activity of these downstream targets, thereby influencing the enzyme's function. This integrated pathway highlights the complexity of the molecular network and underscores the importance of considering indirect relationships in drug-target analysis.",
